WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Can I show you a crazy new AI side

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.240
hustle that's making people rich, which

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.640
can be run as a solo one-person AI

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.760
business by combining Canva with the

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.520
insane power of Claude? Seriously, it's

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.400
pretty cool. As I showcased in my

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.480
previous video on this channel, people

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.840
are using AI to create these super

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.560
popular kids motivational books, which

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.520
are going insanely viral on Amazon. For

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.320
example, you take this creator, who I

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.360
also showed off in that video. They've

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.600
created a series of books for girls and

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.960
boys of all ages. And they're all very

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.200
similar, 12 to 15 short stories, most

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.280
likely AI generated, with images that

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.040
are almost certainly also AI generated.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.720
And they're popular. And to prove it's

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.760
popular, you just have to take the daily

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.680
best seller rank for each book and pop

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.360
it into a sales estimator tool. So, I

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.280
did that. And when I combined each of

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.920
the estimated sales together, it came to

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:56.560
an estimated 16,700

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.160
to 21,000 book sales per month. Kind of

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.400
crazy, right? And you know, I'm 99%

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.000
certain that these books are sold

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.519
through Amazon's self-publish service,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.600
KDP. This lets you upload a PDF and turn

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:08.600
it into a book listing for free. Then,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.480
each time someone buys your book, Amazon

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.000
will print your book on demand for them.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.920
They'll remove the printing fees and pay

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.560
you the profit as royalties. And using

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.720
the KDP fee calculator, we can estimate

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.720
each of these books as earning a $6.64

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.240
royalty. Which, if you do the math,

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.600
works out to be a very nice estimated

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.440
royalty check for this creator, doesn't

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.920
it?

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.000
So, of course, the next question is

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.160
this. How can you now sell your own

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.760
book? And that's a good question, which

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.720
is why in this tutorial, I'll be showing

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.160
you the six steps that you can copy to

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:43.600
research, create, publish, and market

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.520
your own kids book using free traffic.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.880
So then, let's get started with step

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.200
one. Pick a high-demand, low-competition

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.880
niche to get free traffic. So, [music]

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.560
check this out. If we come and do a

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.360
search for generic kids short story

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.720
motivational books, you'll see say there

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.840
is a high demand for them. Lots are

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.800
being sold, but there are also lots of

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.720
competition, too. Which means if you

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.800
just try to copy these, your book will

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.320
most likely get lost in the crowd.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.800
Unless, of course, you're willing to pay

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.920
a lot of money on ads. And don't get me

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.920
wrong, if you have money to spend, it

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.880
could be a good investment because these

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.440
books are SEL products. SEL stands for

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.240
social and emotional learning.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.120
Basically, they're products like books

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.320
and games designed to help kids gain

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.320
emotional intelligence and resilience.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.440
And demand for them is growing. In the

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.840
next 9 years, the market is set to

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.400
quadruple. So, if you do want to invest

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.480
money into competing for the biggest

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.600
generic niches, it might pay off in the

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.560
future. But not everybody has the money

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.520
to pay for ads, and I don't think that

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.640
you need them because this is a big

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:45.440
market, which means niche books aimed at

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.680
niche demographics are selling well, not

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.160
just generic books, such as this one

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.400
aimed at the niche of kids that like

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.120
baseball. So, I thought, "Hmm, why not

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.360
find something else that is popular with

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.080
kids these days and make a motivational

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.440
book themed around it?" So, I came to

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:01.959
the AI chatbot Claude, and I asked,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.720
"What sort of things do kids age 6 to 8

00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:05.560
like right now?" And I turned on high

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.200
effort mode with advanced thinking and

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.959
reasoning turned on to get the best

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.160
answer, and then I submitted it. Now, I

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.760
use Claude because currently it is my

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.200
favorite AI for research. But honestly,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.000
ChatGPT and Gemini are great, too. So,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.840
you can use any that you prefer. You

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.840
don't have to use Claude. But, yes, out

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.280
of these answers that it gave me, this

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.080
one excited me most. The fact that kids

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.519
these days love animals. Since, as my

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:33.680
long-time viewers know, I also love

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:35.519
animals. So, I did a search for kids

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.880
motivational short story books themed

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:41.680
around animals, and guess what? [music]

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:43.880
There were no books. So, you can see the

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.920
opportunity here, right? If we were to

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.760
make a book targeting this niche, then

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:49.800
in theory, it should rise to the top of

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.080
Amazon search engine results for related

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.840
keywords, which in theory would then get

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.720
us free traffic from parents who

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.080
organically discover it while looking

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:01.120
for animal themed SEL books for their

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.840
kid who is obsessed with animals. So,

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.560
now that we have our niche, we can now

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.880
move on to the next step, which is to

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.680
write our short stories. And honestly,

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.920
probably any AI bot will suffice. So, if

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.800
you prefer Gemini or ChatGPT, you can

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.200
use them instead. But currently, my

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.720
favorite AI for writing is also Claude,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:20.720
so I will be using that. So, first up, I

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.520
created a custom project for my new

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.000
book. This is going to make it much

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.623
easier to group all of our chats

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:24.640
together.

00:04:24.623 --> 00:04:26.720
>> [music]

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.880
>> Then inside of this project, I asked it

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.919
to help me create a plan. I explained to

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:32.840
it what my book niche is, who my target

00:04:30.919 --> 00:04:35.160
audience is, and explained that I will

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:37.320
want to create 15 short stories, and

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:39.680
that I wanted it to create a plan on

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:41.560
what topic each short story should be.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.520
And because this wasn't super advanced

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.680
and didn't require complex reasoning, I

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.280
saved my token usage by selecting the

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.520
latest mid-level Claude model, Sonnet,

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:52.200
and selected medium thinking for it. And

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.120
then, that was it. I let it do its

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.000
magic. It took a few minutes, but it was

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.880
well worth it because look what it did.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.000
It turned the story ideas it came up

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:02.280
with into these interactive color-coded

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.240
cards showing what lesson each story

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.000
would be focused on. And it also wrote

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.919
out a description for each story

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.840
explaining what happens in each story

00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:11.840
and themed each story not only around

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.760
specific types of lessons, but also

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:16.200
different types of animals, which was

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:18.240
perfect as that's exactly what I asked

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.360
for. So, since this is pretty much

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.440
exactly what I had wanted, I didn't need

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:24.480
to make any changes to this. So, I just

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:26.919
asked Claude to turn it into a reference

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.760
PDF, which it did, no problem. So, I

00:05:26.919 --> 00:05:30.320
downloaded this PDF, and then I came

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.080
back to the project homepage, and I

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.120
uploaded it inside of the reference

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.400
document section. And then next, it was

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.040
time to write my stories. So, first up,

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.040
I once again explained what my book was

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:42.000
about, and I asked it to write the first

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:44.200
story using the reference file, and I

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.440
also decided to shorten my stories a bit

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.800
down to 4,000 characters since I was

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.640
